{% endif %}
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="quality">
<h2 id="quality">Quality gate</h2>
<p>A cheaper configuration (a quantized checkpoint, a different engine, other engine flags) is only worth ranking if it answers as well as a baseline configuration of the same model. Each candidate is scored on pinned subsets of evaluation tasks, on the same items as its baseline, and the gate compares them per task with a paired bootstrap confidence interval of the score difference (candidate − baseline), so per-item difficulty cancels out.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>pass</strong>: on every task, the lower end of the interval is above the non-inferiority margin, the largest drop accepted.</li>
<li><strong>fail</strong>: on at least one task, the interval lies entirely below that margin. Failing configs are listed with the reason and never ranked, however cheap.</li>
<li><strong>inconclusive</strong>: otherwise; the interval is too wide to decide. The config is shown with that status.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each model page shows every task's score, its interval and the difference from the baseline. A config with no gate decision is shown as "not evaluated".</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="content">
<h2 id="content">Synthetic and realistic content</h2>
<p>Workloads use either synthetic prompts (random words with fixed input and output lengths, so engines are compared on identical shapes) or realistic text from a named dataset. Every result states which. Random text understates the gains from prefix caching and speculative decoding, so a synthetic-content cost can be higher than the same config would achieve on real traffic; realistic content depends on the dataset's mix of lengths. Compare costs only within one workload.</p>
{% if method.datasets %}
<p>Datasets in this snapshot:</p>
<ul>
{% for d in method.datasets %}
<li>{{ d.text }}{% if d.source %}; source: {{ link_list([d.source]) }}{% endif %}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="scope">
<h2 id="scope">What we don't do</h2>
<ul>
<li>We do not benchmark other providers' APIs. Several providers' terms restrict benchmarking their services, so the harness ships no tooling, credentials or presets for third-party endpoints. Competitor numbers are public list prices only, entered by hand with their source and check date. See the <a href="{{ legal_url }}">competitor benchmarking note</a>.</li>
<li>We do not publish raw peak throughput as capacity. Cost is always computed at goodput under the stated SLO.</li>
<li>We do not rank a result that is untrusted or failed the quality gate. It stays on the page with the reason.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="snapshot">
<h2 id="snapshot">This snapshot</h2>
<dl class="defs compact">
<dt>Generated</dt><dd>{{ manifest.generated_at.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC') }} from commit <code>{{ manifest.git.sha or 'not recorded' }}</code></dd>
<dt>Experiments</dt><dd>{% for e in snapshot.experiments %}<a href="{{ root }}data/experiments/{{ e.id }}.json">{{ e.name }}</a> <code>{{ e.id }}</code>{{ '; ' if not loop.last }}{% else %}none yet: first runs pending{% endfor %}</dd>
<dt>SLO</dt><dd>{{ describe_slo(manifest.slo) if manifest.slo else 'none yet: no results published' }}</dd>
<dt>Cost allocation</dt><dd>{{ manifest.allocation or 'none yet: no results published' }}</dd>
<dt>Runs</dt><dd>{{ manifest.run_count }}</dd>
{% if method.content_kinds %}<dt>Content</dt><dd>{{ method.content_kinds|join(', ') }}</dd>{% endif %}
</dl>
<p class="section-note">Everything the site is built from is published as JSON: <a href="{{ root }}data/manifest.json">manifest.json</a>, per-model results under <code>data/models/</code>, and one provenance file per run under <code>data/provenance/</code>.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
